    <!-- vivo 1907N IMS bring-up: WWAN (cellular) DataService/NetworkService already resolve to
         com.android.phone via AOSP's own defaults (config_telephony.xml), which is why
         CellularDataService already worked. WLAN (IWLAN/VoWiFi) has no AOSP default at all -
         these four are the exact values from stock's real framework-res.apk (decoded from the
         real device, not guessed), pointing at the same mediatek-telephony-common.jar classes
         we already ship byte-identical to stock as PRODUCT_BOOT_JARS - see the matching
         <service> entries added to packages/services/Telephony's AndroidManifest.xml. Without
         these, DataServiceManager/AccessNetworksManager can never bind an IWLAN data or network
         service, so VoWiFi can never come up - and per the user's own description of stock's
         actual behavior, VoLTE here apparently never registers cold either; it bootstraps via a
         real VoWiFi registration (connect wifi, wait for the icon, disconnect) which then
         survives the handover back to cellular. If that's really how this carrier/device
         combination works, IWLAN plumbing isn't a separate "later" feature - it may be required
         to get ANY IMS registration at all. -->
    <string name="config_wlan_data_service_class" translatable="false">com.mediatek.internal.telephony.dataconnection.IwlanDataService</string>
    <string name="config_wlan_data_service_package" translatable="false">com.android.phone</string>
    <string name="config_wlan_network_service_class" translatable="false">com.mediatek.internal.telephony.IWlanNetworkService</string>
    <string name="config_wlan_network_service_package" translatable="false">com.android.phone</string>

    <!-- vivo 1907N IMS bring-up: the actual missing piece, found via a live dumpsys check
         against a real stock Funtouch log (~/fp_and_ims_logcat.txt, MtkQualifiedNetworksService
         logging "UPDATE_QUALIFIED_NETWORKS" every few seconds throughout, from the very start).
         On our build the equivalent never bound at all - `dumpsys activity services` showed
         IWlanNetworkService/IwlanDataService genuinely bound, but no ServiceRecord for
         MtkQualifiedNetworksService, ever, in any capture. Root cause: unlike
         config_wwan_data_service_package (defaults to com.android.phone in AOSP's own
         config_telephony.xml), config_qualified_networks_service_package has NO AOSP default at
         all - it's an empty string unless a device overlay sets it, by design (its own code
         comment: "Return empty string when in legacy mode"). The earlier patch adding
         MtkQualifiedNetworksService's <service> manifest entry never added this override,
         wrongly assuming an empty package would resolve the same way an empty *class* name does
         (implicit intent) - AccessNetworksManager.bindQualifiedNetworksService() logs exactly
         "Can't find the binding package" and returns immediately when the package itself is
         empty, before ever constructing an intent at all. Stock's own framework-res.apk sets
         this to com.android.phone (confirmed by decoding it directly) - same value as the WLAN
         entries above, since MtkQualifiedNetworksService lives in the same
         mediatek-telephony-common.jar, hosted the same way inside com.android.phone. -->
    <string name="config_qualified_networks_service_package" translatable="false">com.android.phone</string>
</resources>
